    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-192c0093cd7c-0000-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 14,
                "start": 14
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioner argued that the phrase \u201cother law enforcement officer\u201d should be read broadly to include any loose tax or customs function."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Shanmugam",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-192c0093cd7c-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 38,
                "start": 38
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Shanmugam, counsel for the petitioner contended that an officer acting in a customs or tax capacity is actually acting in a revenue\u2011collecting capacity, and that under the petitioner\u2019s construction the statutory phrase \u201cany officer of customs or excise\u201d should not be limited to a revenue\u2011collecting function."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner (Ali)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Andre",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-192c0093cd7c-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 52,
                "start": 52
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Andre, government counsel argued that the statutory language is clear and that the phrase \u201cany other\u201d followed by \u201cany worker engaged in interstate or foreign commerce\u201d has a plain meaning in context."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Andre",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-192c0093cd7c-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 55,
                "start": 55
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Andre, counsel noted that even if a prisoner obtains In Forma Pauperis (IFP) status, the filing fee must still be paid, albeit in installments, and that the plaintiff must consider the cost\u2011benefit of suing."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Andre",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-192c0093cd7c-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 55,
                "start": 55
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Andre, counsel further explained that the amount at stake ($177) may not justify litigation, especially when filing fees were lower in earlier years."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent (Federal Bureau of Prisons)",
